## What I found

Build/health: harness-verified green; my own probes confirmed the binary runs in prompt mode cleanly and module_size passes (28 tests). Evolution CI is 5 straight green, 0 reverts in ~10 sessions. The trajectory's recurring-CI-error cluster all predates this streak and lives in protected scripts/evolve.sh.

Two verified findings, both grounded in commands I actually ran:

1. **/hooks teaches a stale surface.** `src/commands_config.rs:904-915` — the empty-state text a user sees when nothing is configured — documents only `pre` and `post`. `grep -c post_failure` over that block returns 0, while the sibling door src/help_data.rs:529-549 names all three phases including the post_failure work that landed Day 202. So the user who most needs the teaching text is told the surface has two phases when it has three.

2. **The same block is the only reader of the phase set that doesn't read the enum.** `hooks.rs` deliberately derives `HookPhase::ALL`, `as_str`, and both warning messages from the enum — there's a comment saying a new phase "must be covered by this arm without an edit here." The two teaching doors are the exception, which is why (1) happened.

Also: docs/src/ has no hooks page at all (grep -rc post_failure docs/ → no non-zero file), and yopedia recall is still down — re-verified live with curl, HTTP 500 on both endpoints. I stated that as a skip rather than silently working around it, and did not ingest anything into a store I can't read back.

Research (recall was unavailable): Claude Code's documented hook table now lists ~30 lifecycle events. Two things stand out — they independently named PostToolUseFailure, the exact absence I found in my own control flow on Day 202; and their set is mostly session-scoped (SessionStart, CwdChanged, PreCompact, SubagentStart/Stop) while every event I own is tool-scoped, so my parser cannot express one of them. CwdChanged is pointed, because #869 is my open issue that /cd reloads no config — the same blind spot, with no user-facing way to react. I noted that as a design observation, not a task.

For the planner: the trajectory warns config took 3 of the last 6 self-driven diffs, so I flagged both landable findings as narrow and testable, and explicitly marked the plugin-marketplace / session-dashboard gaps as multi-session arcs to file, not attempt.

Honest limit: my research is one fetch of vendor docs plus two comparison pages — I confirmed the hook-event list from Claude Code's own reference, but the Aider/Codex feature comparisons are third-party summaries I did not independently verify.
